592 - Watchman, Tell Us of the Night
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 592
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Dm/F]Watchman, [Am]tell us of [Dm/A]the [C/G]night
[Dm/A]What its [Am]signs of [Dm/A]promise [A]are.
[Am/E]Traveler, o’er yon mountain’s height,
[Dm/A]See [Edim]that [Dm/F]glory [Am]beaming star.
[Dm/A]Watchman, does its [F]beauteous [C/G]ray
[Dm/A]Aught [C7/Bb]of joy [Dm/A]or hope [Am]foretell?
[F]Traveler, [Am]yes; [Dm/F]it [Bb]brings the [C]day,
[F/A]Promised [Gm/D]day of [Gbm/Db]Israel.

Verse 2:
[Dm/F]Watchman, [Am]tell us of the night, higher yet [Dm/A]that [C/G]star ascends.
[Am/E]Traveler, [Dm/A]blessedness and light, [Am/E]peace and truth its course portends.
[Dm/A]Watchman, [C7/Bb]will its beams [Dm/A]alone gild [Am]the spot [Dm/A]that [C/E]gave them birth?
[F/A]Traveler, ages [Gm/D]are its own; See it [Gbm/Db]bursts o'er all the earth.

Verse 3:
[Dm/F]Watchman, [Am]tell us of the night, for the morning [C/G]seems to [Dm/F]dawn.
[Am/E]Traveler, darkness takes [Dm/F]its [Am/E]flight, doubt and terror are withdrawn.
[Dm/A]Watchman, [C7/Bb]let your wanderings [Dm/A]cease; [Am]hasten [Dm/A]to [C/E]your quiet home.
[F/A]Traveler, lo, the [Gm/D]Prince of Peace, lo, the [Gbm/Db]Son of God is come!
